VeridianOS: expmed: read op0_mode directly in extract_bit_field_1

GCC reported:

  gcc/expmed.cc:1864:45: warning: '*(unsigned int*)((char*)&imode +
    offsetof(scalar_int_mode, scalar_int_mode::m_mode))' may be used
    uninitialized [-Wmaybe-uninitialized]

A false positive: imode is only used after op0_mode.exists (&imode) has
returned true, and that call stores it.  The optimiser cannot follow the
conditional store through the earlier, partly overlapping uses of the
same variable (giving the second check its own variable still warns).
The subreg check now tests op0_mode.exists () and passes
op0_mode.require (), the same mode exists (&imode) stored, so no
possibly-unset variable is involved.  No behaviour change.

diff -ru a/gcc/expmed.cc b/gcc/expmed.cc
--- a/gcc/expmed.cc	2026-08-07 03:46:06.148689668 -0400
+++ b/gcc/expmed.cc	2026-10-08 17:04:51.646148293 -0400
@@ -1859,9 +1859,9 @@
   /* Extraction of a full MODE1 value can be done with a subreg as long
      as the least significant bit of the value is the least significant
      bit of either OP0 or a word of OP0.  */
-  if (!MEM_P (op0) && !reverse && op0_mode.exists (&imode))
+  if (!MEM_P (op0) && !reverse && op0_mode.exists ())
     {
-      rtx sub = extract_bit_field_as_subreg (mode1, op0, imode,
+      rtx sub = extract_bit_field_as_subreg (mode1, op0, op0_mode.require (),
 					     bitsize, bitnum);
       if (sub)
 	return convert_extracted_bit_field (sub, mode, tmode, unsignedp);
